---
description: Design and accessibility rules for UI components
globs: src/components/**/*.tsx, src/app/**/*.tsx, src/app/globals.css
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use the design tokens from `src/app/globals.css` (`paper`, `surface`, `ink`,
  `muted`, `line`, `accent`, `signal`). No raw hex values in components.
- Verify light and dark themes, and mobile (390px) as well as desktop.
- Semantic HTML first: landmarks, one `h1` per page, ordered headings, real
  `<button>` and `<a>` elements, visible focus.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Motion only answers a user action or marks
  one deliberate moment.
- Prefer `<ViewTransition>` from React for route animations; see the
  `vercel-react-view-transitions` skill.
- Keep the axe e2e test (`e2e/site.spec.ts`) green.
